      "side": 1,
      "message": "I spoke to a friend of mine on the Android compiler team about this prior to writing up this CL. He said we could do one of the following:\n1. Move away from hard into softfp which gives us a small performance hit, but he assured me that as long as we\u0027re not doing any tight recursion or using a very tight loop in which we pass floats as function arguments it won\u0027t be that bad.\n2. Use a pointer to the float when using varargs and keep everything else the same.\n\nHis recommendation was to go with #2 since we\u0027re rarely ever going to be using varargs with floats. I feel like moving to softfp is an entirely different discussion and we\u0027d need to do a TON of validating before committing to such a change.",
